t/conception-technique.md` §4.1.\n108\t- Never let an unqualified sandbox backend run unconfined. Refuse with `capability_missing` instead.\n109\t\n110\t## Agent Rules\n111\t\n112\t- **The cycle:** a change goes through the six steps of `cycle/README.md` — story, red-green,\n113\t  self-review, review, acceptance run, landing — driven by the tool of `cycle/`; a step the tool does\n114\t  not cover yet is done by hand, in that order and under those rules.\n115\t- **Red before code:** a task says what its test asserts in the words of the story and why that\n116\t  fails today; the test is written first and seen failing on that assertion before the code.\n117\t- **Review:** two reviewers, two rounds at most, on the promises of the story; what the second\n118\t  round leaves goes to `specs/bugs/registry.yaml`, except a promise the code does not keep, which\n119\t  the owner decides.\n120\t- **Acceptance run:** a real execution in a real Pi, with a negative control; a list backed by tests\n121\t  is not one.\n122\t- **Always Green:** Preflight (`npm run check`) is green before forward work and before every\n123\t  commit that touches what it checks.\n124\t- **Records:** the story, a product decision, a registry entry and the plan are written by hand;\n125\t  every red, Preflight, review round and acceptance is observed and written once by the tool.\n126\t- Write the minimum code that solves the stated problem.\n127\t- Run tests after every change. Show evidence before declaring done.\n128\t\n129\t## Token Economy — Minimal Footprint\n130\t\n131\t> Production-safe subset of the 8-rule AGENTS.md pattern (Vercel engineer, ~60B tokens).\n132\t> Rule 1 (\"no backward compatibility\") is excluded deliberately: it risks data loss in production.\n133\t\n134\t1. **Check existing dependencies first.** DO inspect what your current dependencies already do before adding a package or writing your own code.\n135\t2. **Prefer mature, maintained libraries.** DO NOT rewrite a capability a